s} ___ my arm when I was ten.", "verbs": ["break"], "persons": ["I"]}, {"id": "present", "text": "{s} ___ my sister a present for Christmas.", "verbs": ["give"], "persons": ["I"]}, {"id": "snow", "text": "Last winter {s} ___ in the snow many times.", "verbs": ["fall"]}, {"id": "fun", "text": "{s} ___ a lot of fun at the camp.", "verbs": ["have"]}, {"id": "test", "text": "{s} ___ the maths test very quickly.", "verbs": ["do"]}, {"id": "tired", "text": "After the hike {s} ___ very tired.", "verbs": ["feel"]}]},
    {"id": "present-perfect", "name": "Present perfect / past simple", "rule": "Zeitpunkt genannt → past simple; bis jetzt (ever, yet) → have/has + 3. Form", "kind": "choice", "items": [{"id": "1", "text": "I ___ to London last summer.", "answers": ["went"], "wrong": ["have been", "have gone", "go"], "hint": "(go)"}, {"id": "2", "text": "Have you ever ___ sushi?", "answers": ["eaten"], "wrong": ["ate", "eat", "eated"], "hint": "(eat)"}, {"id": "3", "text": "She ___ her keys. Now she can't open the door.", "answers": ["has lost"], "wrong": ["lost", "have lost", "loses"], "hint": "(lose)"}, {"id": "4", "text": "We ___ that film yesterday.", "answers": ["saw"], "wrong": ["have seen", "has seen", "see"], "hint": "(see)"}, {"id": "5", "text": "I ___ on a plane.", "answers": ["have never been"], "wrong": ["never was", "has never been", "am never"], "hint": "(never · be)"}, {"id": "6", "text": "Tom ___ his homework yet.", "answers": ["hasn't finished", "has not finished"], "wrong": ["didn't finish", "haven't finished", "not finished"], "hint": "(not finish)"}, {"id": "7", "text": "My parents ___ in Geneva in 2010.", "answers": ["met"], "wrong": ["have met", "has met", "meet"], "hint": "(meet)"}, {"id": "8", "text": "Look! I ___ a new phone.", "answers": ["have just bought"], "wrong": ["just bought", "has just bought", "just buyed"], "hint": "(just · buy)"}, {"id": "9", "text": "When ___ your bike?", "answers": ["did you get"], "wrong": ["have you got", "has you got", "you got"], "hint": "(you · get)"}, {"id": "10", "text": "___ your room yet?", "answers": ["Have you cleaned"], "wrong": ["Did you cleaned", "Has you cleaned", "Are you cleaned"], "hint": "(you · clean)"}, {"id": "11", "text": "He ___ the piano for two years when he was little.", "answers": ["played"], "wrong": ["has played", "have played", "plays"], "hint": "(play)"}, {"id": "12", "text": "I ___ Anna since Monday.", "answers": ["haven't seen", "have not seen"], "wrong": ["didn't see", "don't see", "hasn't seen"], "hint": "(not see)"}, {"id": "13", "text": "Yesterday we ___ a long walk.", "answers": ["took"], "wrong": ["have taken", "has taken", "take"], "hint": "(take)"}, {"id": "14", "text": "She ___ three books this month.", "answers": ["has read"], "wrong": ["readed", "have read", "reads"], "hint": "(read)"}, {"id": "15", "text": "Oh no, it ___ to rain!", "answers": ["has started"], "wrong": ["started", "have started", "starts"], "hint": "(start)"}, {"id": "16", "text": "What ___ last weekend?", "answers": ["did you do"], "wrong": ["have you done", "has you done", "you did"], "hint": "(you · do)"}, {"id": "17", "text": "They ___ in this house since 2015.", "answers": ["have lived"], "wrong": ["lived", "has lived", "live"], "hint": "(live)"}, {"id": "18", "text": "Mozart ___ his first symphony at the age of eight.", "answers": ["wrote"], "wrong": ["has written", "have written", "writes"], "hint": "(write)"}, {"id": "19", "text": "I can't find my pencil. ___ it?", "answers": ["Have you seen"], "wrong": ["Did you seen", "Has you seen", "Are you seen"], "hint": "(you · see)"}]},
    {"id": "will-going-to", "name": "will / going to", "rule": "Plan oder sichtbares Zeichen → going to; spontan, Versprechen, Vermutung → will", "kind": "choice", "items": [{"id": "1", "text": "Look at those clouds! It ___ rain.", "answers": ["is going to"], "wrong": ["will to", "goes to", "is going"]}, {"id": "2", "text": "We have bought the tickets. We ___ visit Paris in May.", "answers": ["are going to"], "wrong": ["will to", "go to", "are go to"]}, {"id": "3", "text": "The phone is ringing. – I ___ answer it!", "answers": ["will", "'ll"], "wrong": ["am going", "going to", "will to"]}, {"id": "4", "text": "I think Switzerland ___ win the match.", "answers": ["will"], "wrong": ["is going", "will to", "goes to"]}, {"id": "5", "text": "Don't worry, I ___ tell anybody.", "answers": ["won't", "will not"], "wrong": ["don't", "am not going", "not will"]}, {"id": "6", "text": "She has her bag packed. She ___ leave.", "answers": ["is going to"], "wrong": ["will to", "going to", "is go to"]}, {"id": "7", "text": "Maybe it ___ be sunny tomorrow.", "answers": ["will"], "wrong": ["is going", "will to", "goes"]}, {"id": "8", "text": "What ___ you going to do after school?", "answers": ["are"], "wrong": ["will", "do", "is"]}, {"id": "9", "text": "I'm hungry. – I ___ make you a sandwich.", "answers": ["will", "'ll"], "wrong": ["am going", "going to", "will to"]}, {"id": "10", "text": "Next year my brother ___ start an apprenticeship.", "answers": ["is going to"], "wrong": ["will to", "going to", "is go"]}, {"id": "11", "text": "Careful! You ___ fall!", "answers": ["are going to"], "wrong": ["will to", "going", "are go"]}, {"id": "12", "text": "I promise I ___ be on time.", "answers": ["will"], "wrong": ["am going", "will to", "going to"]}, {"id": "13", "text": "In 2050 people ___ live on the moon, perhaps.", "answers": ["will"], "wrong": ["are going", "will to", "goes to"]}, {"id": "14", "text": "We ___ have a party on Saturday. Do you want to come?", "answers": ["are going to"